{"claim": "dev.git landed (bricks 1+2, commit 8f0ba1bc, branch claude/git-first-class): git is a first-class platform surface driven off a repo registry at runtime/dev/repos.json, split into three mode wrappers over one no-shell argv engine.", "detail": "set_repo/remove_repo/repos manage the registry (canon and newbound-agent registered with origins and roles). dev.git.read is the free read-only surface (status/log/diff/show/...); dev.git.write covers local mutation (add/commit/checkout/...) and supplies a neutral identity when the repo has none; dev.git.remote_op (fetch/pull/push) defaults pull to --ff-only unless a strategy flag is stated - the ff-only rule done by mechanism instead of parsing English. gitrun is the internal engine: per-mode verb allowlist, argv form, one system_call, nothing interpolated. Verified live by using the new tools themselves to inspect canon post-crash.", "tags": "dev.git,git,registry,repos.json,first-class-surface,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787314650562},
{"claim": "gitrun's neutral-identity fallback is gated on verb == \"commit\" only, so any commit-creating verb like merge (or revert) on a box with no git user.email configured fails with git's raw 'Please tell me who you are' lecture - update_from_master and merge_to_master surface it at their merge step.", "detail": "Verified live: re-running the merge directly through dev-git-write hit the identical refusal; the repo was left clean, nothing half-merged. The autocommit sweeper never trips this because it only issues commit, where the fallback works. Box-side workaround: git config --global user.name/user.email (one-time). Durable fix is widening the fallback in gitrun to every commit-creating verb - a newbound_core change (host rebuild + restart), so not done on a live instance.", "tags": "dev.git,gitrun,merge,identity,update_from_master,gotcha,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1790261004587},
{"claim": "On autocommit repos the sweeper races deliberate commits - it can commit and push generated sources before you fold them into your own commit", "detail": "A store edit regenerates rust source in the library repo; the 5-minute autocommit_sweep may commit and push that generated file before a deliberate hand commit includes it, splitting one logical change across two commits. Since the sweeper's commit is already pushed, do not rewrite history: verify the trees are identical and reset the local branch onto origin, keeping the sweeper's commit. To avoid the race, commit immediately after the store edit or flip the repo's autocommit off (dev.git.set_autocommit) for the duration of deliberate commit work.", "tags": "dev.git,autocommit,workflow,oneshot,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1792772434104},
{"claim": "commit_unit's closure misses an FFI-crate library's generated command sources", "detail": "dev.git.commit_unit gathers generated rust only under newbound_core/src/<lib>/<ctl>/; for an FFI-crate library the generated source lives in the library's own crate (e.g. gudrun/src/gudrun/gudrun/status.rs in the oneshot repo) and falls outside the unit, so it needs its own follow-up commit. Hit twice on 2026-10-25 (status.rs, google_callback.rs each committed separately after commit_unit).", "tags": "dev.git,commit_unit,ffi,gudrun,oneshot,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1792926391169},
{"end": true}]
